<p>Utility classes for spacing, sizing, display, flexbox, text, colour, borders, and more.
    Most ship from <code>@keenmate/pure-css</code>; the rest from core. For heights in real
    layouts see <a href="/layout/sizing">Sizing &amp; Layout</a>, for text styles
    <a href="/design/typography">Typography</a>, for the 1&ndash;9 colour slots
    <a href="/design/colors">Colors</a>.</p>

<!-- Spacing -->
<div class="pa-card">
    <div class="pa-card__header">
        <div class="pa-card__title">
            <h3 class="pa-card__title-text">Spacing - Margin &amp; Padding</h3>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pa-card__body">
        <h4>Two scales</h4>
        <table class="pa-table pa-table--striped pa-table--sm mb-4">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Scale</th>
                    <th>Steps</th>
                    <th>Values</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Numeric</td>
                    <td><code>0</code>&ndash;<code>6</code>, <code>8</code>, <code>10</code>, <code>12</code>, <code>16</code>, <code>20</code> (no 7, 9, 11&hellip;)</td>
                    <td>0 / .25 / .5 / .75 / 1 / 1.25 / 1.5 / 2 / 2.5 / 3 / 4 / 5 rem</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Semantic</td>
                    <td><code>0</code>, <code>xs</code>, <code>sm</code>, <code>md</code>, <code>base</code>, <code>lg</code>, <code>xl</code>, <code>2xl</code></td>
                    <td>0 / .4 / .8 / 1.2 / 1.6 / 2.4 / 3.2 / 4.8 rem</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h4>Sides</h4>
        <table class="pa-table pa-table--striped pa-table--sm mb-4">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Sides</th>
                    <th>Margin</th>
                    <th>Padding</th>
                    <th>Scales</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>All / axis</td>
                    <td><code>m-*</code>, <code>mx-*</code>, <code>my-*</code></td>
                    <td><code>p-*</code>, <code>px-*</code>, <code>py-*</code></td>
                    <td>numeric + semantic</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Top / bottom</td>
                    <td><code>mt-*</code>, <code>mb-*</code></td>
                    <td><code>pt-*</code>, <code>pb-*</code></td>
                    <td>numeric + semantic</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Start / end</td>
                    <td><code>ms-*</code>, <code>me-*</code></td>
                    <td><code>ps-*</code>, <code>pe-*</code></td>
                    <td>numeric + semantic</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <div class="pa-callout pa-callout--info mb-4">
            <div class="pa-callout__content">
                <p>Horizontal sides are <strong>start / end</strong>: they follow the writing
                    direction, so under <code>dir="rtl"</code> the spacing mirrors with the layout
                    (<code>ms-*</code> is the left in LTR, the right in RTL). There are no
                    <code>ml-*</code> / <code>mr-*</code> / <code>pl-*</code> / <code>pr-*</code> classes.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <h4>Auto Margins</h4>
        <p class="text-sm mb-4">
            <code>m-auto</code>, <code>mx-auto</code>, <code>my-auto</code>, <code>mt-auto</code>, <code>mb-auto</code>,
            <code>ms-auto</code>, <code>me-auto</code>
        </p>

        <h4>Live Examples</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-2"><code>ms-auto</code> pushes an item to the end of a flex row (the start in RTL):</p>
        <div class="d-flex mb-4" style="background: var(--pc-subtle-bg); padding: 1rem;">
            <span class="pa-badge pa-badge--success">normal</span>
            <span class="pa-badge pa-badge--primary ms-auto">ms-auto (pushed to end)</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-2">Semantic padding:</p>
        <div class="d-flex gap-md flex-wrap align-items-start">
            <div class="p-xs" style="background: var(--pc-primary-bg-subtle);">p-xs</div>
            <div class="p-sm" style="background: var(--pc-primary-bg-subtle);">p-sm</div>
            <div class="p-md" style="background: var(--pc-primary-bg-subtle);">p-md</div>
            <div class="p-lg" style="background: var(--pc-primary-bg-subtle);">p-lg</div>
            <div class="p-xl" style="background: var(--pc-primary-bg-subtle);">p-xl</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Gap Utilities -->
